{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdPYdY8dkjA2GHawsyrd9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VfPLqKM5jNxb94CPKwZ3k7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/arena-ws.hADBMl/SOLUTION.md","content":"# Solution\n\nTwo bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:\n\n1. **`get` did not count as a \"use\".** It read the value out of the `OrderedDict`\n   without calling `move_to_end`, so the recency order only ever reflected writes.\n   A key that was repeatedly read still looked least-recently-used and got evicted.\n   Fixed by moving the key to the end on a successful (non-expired) `get`.\n\n2. **`put` evicted on updates to existing keys.** The capacity check ran before\n   checking whether the key was already present, so overwriting an existing key\n   at full capacity dropped an unrelated entry (and left the cache under capacity).\n   Fixed by only evicting when the key is genuinely new.\n\n`python3 -m pytest -q` now passes (6 passed).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":160,"cache_read_input_tokens":22609,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":160,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":72,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b877f966-8a3c-4934-8a8f-ac35114aafe0","uuid":"d4dcf286-6f57-4421-b6c9-8f48d1654ada","timestamp":"2026-07-25T22:14:26.443Z","request_id":"req_011CdPYdXJ2VvHf3YvDZ7u5V"}
